**Read:** [Mineralogy — Dexter Perkins, open editions](../sources/Mineralogy-Perkins.lingua#r_3Y3EJ93EG4V7Q0TZBCRRXVNVKP), the complete book; [Petrology — Dexter Perkins, open textbook](../sources/Petrology-Perkins.lingua#r_6P7JBVJJ3P1BT6QKDGC7BN6VWV), the complete book; [Guide to Thin Section Microscopy — Raith, Raase, and Reinhardt](../sources/Guide-to-Thin-Section-Microscopy.lingua#r_2MH30T4MGW8YMVP9SA3Z7XCDSD), the entire guide; [Raman Spectroscopy for Mineral Identification — Bartholomew and Post](../sources/Raman-Mineral-Identification-Practical-Guide.lingua#r_3TQHZH1T2CDCQPTVVXSKJ5DCED), the entire guide; [Advanced Igneous Petrology — Timothy Grove, MIT 12.490](../sources/MIT-Advanced-Igneous-Petrology.lingua#r_3R0PJP97ZPE1RSGPPGY8WXXQZF), the full graduate case sequence; [O uso de pseudosseções em Petrologia Metamórfica — Gengo and colleagues](../sources/Pseudossecoes-Gengo-Santos-Moraes-Szabo.lingua#r_00V3DDNE7B5SQHWP5NKFT0YJZR), the complete article.

Completion requires a connected explanation of mineral species/composition/structure, crystallographic geometry/symmetry, substitution/defects, physical/optical properties, analytical methods, phase relations, and igneous/sedimentary/metamorphic histories. Complete the substantial books, courses, manuals, method papers, and research reading assigned through the progression.

Demonstrate suitable specimen and microscope work, calibrated quantitative observation, identification with alternatives, and traceable domain/context handling. Distinguish actual instrument/practical abilities from document, virtual, or supplied-data analysis. Independently derive and check the original formula, diffraction/optical, phase, partitioning, and reaction examples.

Present the sustained analytical/crystallographic, igneous, sedimentary, metamorphic, and feedstock projects with complete methods, independent tests, uncertainty, and substantive revisions after critique. The independent investigation should defend a specific result, acknowledge nonuniqueness, and propose a feasible next study.

Readiness for further work includes identifying what new observations, calibration, models, equipment, or supervision a question needs. Mineralogy/petrology is shared knowledge for geochemistry, materials, economic geology, mining/beneficiation, refining, environmental and planetary work; it does not claim all those specialist designs or operations.

**Work:** defend one integrated material or rock-history account from observations through structure/composition and physical/chemical models to a testable conclusion. Respond to a serious alternative using specific evidence. Continue through [Earth — materials, processes, and geological history](../../Earth.lingua#r_5H7Y6QD1FW4Z0JJ6C7SH4DDHXH), [Chemistry — substances, transformations, and evidence](../../../../stem/chemistry/Chemistry.lingua#r_2NWJY1HCKPBM4T6YQSDHN8S3S0), [STEM — mathematics, science, and engineering](../../../../stem/STEM.lingua#r_4B137J3ZBVM7TD2NA797H2CZ7E), or [Ergon](../../../../ergon/Ergon.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001) for another connected question. These are ordinary reading links and content expectations, with no new automatic completion or software gate.

**Return:** [Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN).
